<title>FRANCE: Ciments Francais Q1 sales rose 5.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Ciments Francais Q1 sales rose 5.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					2,531    vs   2,400</p>
<p>	 - France				   1,288    vs   1,327</p>
<p>	 - EU excluding France		    443    vs     430</p>
<p>	 - Other countries			  800    vs     643</p>
<p>Breakdown by sector</p>
<p>	 - Cement				   1,586    vs    1,442</p>
<p>	 - Construction materials		 945    vs	958</p>
<p>NOTE: Ciments Francais gave the results in a statement. It said sales rose 5.5 percent compared with the same period a year ago. Sales rose 6.6 percent on a comparable size and exchange rate basis.</p>
<p>The company said the growth of international business operations, particularly in North America, Turkey and Morocco more than offset the decline in French and Belgium markets. The Spanish market showed a slight recovery.</p>
<p>The group said it was hard to analyse the performance of the first quarter due to the weight of weather conditions but said the sales rise allowed it to be confident over prospects for the year 1997.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
